{
  "_name": "r4_data_diff_bernoulli",
  "_desc": "R3.x lossy gate (BERNOULLI, distribution sample) — drive via tools/dm_diff_band.py --band <calibrated> --funnel report. alice sends N msgs to bob over a link with per-frame Bernoulli loss, so RTS/CTS/DATA/ACK are stochastically dropped and the retry paths fire repeatedly. Unlike the FORCED gate (deterministic single retry, band 0), here the shared-_rng loss stream diverges across engines, so this is a DISTRIBUTION band — calibrate the tolerance from a multi-seed sweep before locking it as a hard gate (R3.x pin P2). NOT wired into run_tests; a manual/calibration tool. The EWMA data-SF divergence (lua picks data SF by SNR; the C++ port pins data_sf, the EWMA deferred) means a lost CTS desyncs the SF, so expect a non-trivial band. Not runnable directly (nodes carry no engine/script).",
